antaginfo-sunwalker-title = You are the Sunwalker

antaginfo-sunwalker-intro-1 = You are an ancient voidwalker, having been caught in a supernova. You are altered, and hateful.

antaginfo-sunwalker-intro-2 = There will be no lessons or enlightenment, they wont survive to learn from it.

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-space_dive-name = Space Dive

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-space_dive-desc = You can move under the station from space, use this to hunt and get to isolated sections of space.

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-burning_slash-name = Burning Slash

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-burning_slash-desc = Your attacks deal great burn damage and ignite those hit.

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-burning_physiology-name = Burning Physiology

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-burning_physiology-desc = Your very skin heats the air around you, while the vacuum of space mends any wounds your body might have sustained. You can move through glass freely, but are slowed in gravity.

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-stellar_charge-name = Stellar Charge

antaginfo-sunwalker-power-stellar_charge-desc = With an exploding burning speed, charge forwards, dealing damage and burning the surroundings.

antaginfo-nightmare-title = You are a Nightmare.

antaginfo-nightmare-intro-pre = You are a creature from beyond the stars that has incredibly strong powers in the darkness, becoming nigh unbeatable. Unfortunately, you wither and burn away in the light. You must use your

antaginfo-nightmare-intro-light-eater = light eater

antaginfo-nightmare-intro-post = to dim the station, making hunting easier.

antaginfo-nightmare-tip-1-label = Tip #1:

antaginfo-nightmare-tip-1 = Move often. The station will be hunting you after you are discovered, so don't stay in one area for long.

antaginfo-nightmare-tip-2-label = Tip #2:

antaginfo-nightmare-tip-2 = Pick unfair fights. You are incredibly strong in one versus one situations, use it. The more you fight, the harder it will be to keep it dark.

antaginfo-nightmare-tip-3-label = Tip #3:

antaginfo-nightmare-tip-3 = Fully destroy APCs when possible. Instead of hunting lights that can be fixed, hunt the APCs which are harder to repair.

antaginfo-nightmare-power-shadow_dance-name = Shadow Dance

antaginfo-nightmare-power-shadow_dance-desc = Whilst in the shadows, you are immune to all ranged attacks, whilst also rapidly regenerating health.

antaginfo-nightmare-power-shadow_walk-name = Shadow Walk

antaginfo-nightmare-power-shadow_walk-desc = You are allowed unlimited, unrestricted movement in the dark. Light will pull you out of this.

antaginfo-nightmare-power-heart_of_darkness-name = Heart of Darkness

antaginfo-nightmare-power-heart_of_darkness-desc = Your heart invites the shadows. If you die in the darkness, you will eventually revive if left alone.

antaginfo-nightmare-power-light_eater-name = Light Eater

antaginfo-nightmare-power-light_eater-desc = Your twisted appendage. It will consume the light of what it touches, be it victim or object. After 7 seconds of being in jaunt, stabbing a foe will stun them or do extra damage.

antaginfo-voidwalker-title = You are the Voidwalker

antaginfo-voidwalker-intro = You are a creature from the void between stars. You were attracted to the radio signals being broadcasted by this station.

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-survive-label = Survive:

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-survive = You have unrivaled freedom. Remain in space and no one can stop you. You can move through windows, so stay near them to always have a way out.

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-hunt-label = Hunt:

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-hunt = Pick unfair fights. Look for inattentive targets and strike at them when they don't expect you.

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-abduct-label = Abduct:

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-abduct = Your Unsettle ability stuns and drains your targets. Knock them out with your draining slash, take them to space (or nebula vomit) and enlighten them.

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-reap-label = Reap:

antaginfo-voidwalker-tip-reap = Our students expell our essence regularly. We can use this to go where we could otherwise not, but we reabsorb this when we use it to leave. (You can dive in space vomit.)

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-space_dive-name = Space Dive

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-space_dive-desc = You can move under the station from space, use this to hunt and get to isolated sections of space.

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-draining_slash-name = Draining Slash

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-draining_slash-desc = You take the breath right from their lungs and quickly take down even the strongest opponents. Should they resist, right-click allows you to do some raw damage. Your arms are otherwise not very sophisticated, and are not good for much more than just grabbing things.

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-cosmic_physiology-name = Cosmic Physiology

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-cosmic_physiology-desc = Your natural camouflage makes you invisible in space, as well as mending any wounds your body might have sustained. You can move through glass freely, but are slowed in gravity.

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-unsettle-name = Unsettle

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-unsettle-desc = Target a victim while remaining only partially in their view to stun and weaken them, but also announce them your presence.

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-cosmic_dash-name = Cosmic Dash

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-cosmic_dash-desc = With a short range and negligible damage, it makes for a poor offensive tool, but great for quick escapes and repositions.

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-expand-name = Expand

antaginfo-voidwalker-power-expand-desc = For every lesson we teach, we grow in power. We can convert walls into glass to allow us to reach even further.

antaginfo-demon-goals = It is in your nature to accomplish these goals:

antaginfo-demon-powers = Demonic Powers

antaginfo-demon-jaunt-name = Blood Jaunt:

antaginfo-demon-jaunt-desc = You can dive in and out of blood to travel anywhere you need to be. You will gain a speed boost upon leaving the jaunt for surprise attacks. You can drag victims you have disabled through the blood, consuming them and restoring health.

antaginfo-demon-strike-name = Monstrous strike:

antaginfo-demon-strike-desc = You can launch a devastating slam attack by right-clicking, capable of smashing bones in one strike. Great for preventing the escape of your victims, as their wounds will slow them.

antaginfo-glitch-crime-name = Bitrunning

antaginfo-glitch-crime-mid = is a crime. Your mission:

antaginfo-glitch-eliminate = Eliminate

antaginfo-glitch-crime-post = organic intruders to maintain the integrity of the system.

antaginfo-glitch-police-pre = To assist your task, your program has been loaded with cutting edge

antaginfo-glitch-police-skills = martial arts

antaginfo-glitch-police-post = skills.

antaginfo-glitch-police-ranged-pre = Ranged weaponry is

antaginfo-glitch-police-forbidden = forbidden

antaginfo-glitch-police-ranged-post = . Ballistic defense is frowned upon. Style is paramount.

antaginfo-glitch-tac-pre = You are an advanced combat unit. You have been outfitted with

antaginfo-glitch-tac-weapons = lethal weaponry

antaginfo-glitch-tac-terminate = Terminate

antaginfo-glitch-tac-cost = organic life at any cost.

antaginfo-glitch-prime = ORGANIC LIFE MUST BE TERMINATED.

antaginfo-bloodworm-title = You are a Blood Worm!

antaginfo-bloodworm-team = Your team status:

antaginfo-bloodworm-team-blood = Total blood consumed: { $count } units

antaginfo-bloodworm-team-reproduced = Total times reproduced: { $count } times

antaginfo-bloodworm-weaknesses = Weaknesses

antaginfo-bloodworm-tips = Tips

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-breathless-name = Breathless

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-breathless-desc = You don't need to breathe. This extends to your hosts as well.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-blood_consumption-name = Blood Consumption

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-blood_consumption-desc = You can grow by using Leech Blood or Invade Corpse to consume blood, but synthetic blood, such as from monkeys, has a limit. You can see blood levels at a glance using your HUD, and examining targets yields advanced information on their blood.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-growth_stages-name = Growth Stages

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-growth_stages-desc = You can track your growth in your status tab. Once you're fully grown, you can incubate in a cocoon to reach the next growth stage. Reaching juvenile lets you spit blood, and adults are extremely strong.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-ventcrawling-name = Ventcrawling

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-ventcrawling-desc = Hatchlings can ventcrawl. Once you grow up, you lose the ability to ventcrawl, becoming reliant on doorcrawling, breaking doors and ID access to move around. Secure a good spot or a host before maturing to a juvenile.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-doorcrawling-name = Doorcrawling

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-doorcrawling-desc = Hatchlings and juveniles can slide under doors, but adults can't, becoming entirely reliant on breaking doors and ID access to move around. Secure a really good spot or a host before maturing to an adult.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-reproduction-name = Reproduction

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-reproduction-desc = Once you enter your final stage of growth as an adult, you can reproduce to create 3 new hatchlings, in exchange for reverting into one yourself.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-parasitism-name = Parasitism

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-parasitism-desc = You have the supernatural ability to turn into blood upon command. This allows you to enter a corpse, taking it as your host.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-regeneration-name = Regeneration

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-regeneration-desc = You slowly heal over time, taking roughly 5 minutes to fully heal from near-death. While in a host, this translates to recovering blood volume over time. You can inject blood into the damaged tissues of your host to rapidly heal them in exchange for your own health.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-life_support-name = Life Support

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-life_support-desc = While inside of a host, your host doesn't need vital organs to survive, except for a brain. Lungs let you speak, and a liver lets you process chems. You can insert organs into your host by picking them up and right-clicking on your host with them. This works for cybernetics too.

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-alien_mind-name = Alien Mind

antaginfo-bloodworm-power-alien_mind-desc = Your mind is not that of a human. You don't experience cravings, fear, sadness or joy from normal sources, even while in a host.

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-extreme_cold-name = Extreme Cold

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-extreme_cold-desc = Your species is highly pressure and cold resistant, but extremely low pressures and temperatures can still harm you. This doesn't apply to you while in a host and you can equip your host with a space suit to protect it too.

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-high_heat-name = High Heat

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-high_heat-desc = Your species is averse to heat and will rapidly burn up in hot environments. Your body is also flammable, so stay away from fires. This weakness applies even while in a host, but can be covered by equipping your host with fire-resistant gear.

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-bleeding-name = Bleeding

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-bleeding-desc = While in a host, you are transformed entirely into blood. This renders you extremely vulnerable to bleeding wounds. When your host bleeds, it directly damages you, and your hosts continue bleeding even while dead. Your hosts also bleed 50% faster than normal people.

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-inferior_biology-name = Inferior Biology

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-inferior_biology-desc = Your hosts lack your advanced senses, leaving them vulnerable to ordinary impediments like darkness and flashbangs. You can use human tools like night-vision goggles, eye protection and ear protection to circumvent this.

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-testing-name = Testing

antaginfo-bloodworm-weakness-testing-desc = The DeForest corporation has engineered single-use devices for detecting blood worms. They can be ordered by security and take no time to use, but using them is painful for the target and they're really expensive.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-stealthy_healing-name = Stealthy Healing

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-stealthy_healing-desc = Using medbay to heal your host instead of spending blood will avoid leaving your host with deathly pale skin. As a bonus, you get to have more blood for spitting and healing later.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-surprise_worms-name = Surprise Worms

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-surprise_worms-desc = You can leave your host to surprise attack people, which is especially effective as an adult. Be sure to block off any paths of escape first, as it takes 3 seconds to leave your host.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-door_stalking-name = Door Stalking

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-door_stalking-desc = As a hatchling or a juvenile, you can slide under a door to stalk nearby victims. Be wary of anyone coming to open the door.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-meatshields-name = Meatshields

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-meatshields-desc = Hosts are practically meatshields for you, just keep track of any fires, bleeding wounds, cremators or gibbing mechanisms. Remember to also heal your host periodically using Inject Blood whenever they get too low.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-life_insurance-name = Life Insurance

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-life_insurance-desc = Because you can't control corpses while you have less than a tenth of your health in blood volume, you will be ejected from your host when you get really low. You can use this as insurance to get a last ditch escape attempt.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-medbay_buffet-name = Medbay Buffet

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-medbay_buffet-desc = Medbay's blood freezers can be a decent source of synthetic blood if you can't find any monkeys. Be careful of nearby crew, as the sounds of breaking freezers can travel through walls.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-fast_food-name = Fast Food

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-fast_food-desc = You can enter corpses to consume all of their blood extremely quickly. Blood gained while already in a host doesn't affect your growth. Duplicated blood does, but it's synthetic, limiting its effectiveness.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-nomadic-name = Nomadic

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-nomadic-desc = You have night vision and no territory, meaning you can thrive anywhere. Hatchlings can ventcrawl, while juveniles and adults can break doors and other obstacles with their bare teeth. Nowhere is safe from you!

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-team_up-name = Team Up

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-team_up-desc = Your kin often share your goals and are willing to work together. You have your own language, Wormspeak, which is only understandable to your kin. You can tell if someone is a blood worm host via a HUD icon.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-jail_time-name = Jail Time

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-jail_time-desc = Sec got you? You can break any restraints on your host, including lockers and such, by right-clicking with Spit Blood active. You can also leave your host and ventcrawl out or break through the door.

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-jumpstart-name = Jumpstart

antaginfo-bloodworm-tip-jumpstart-desc = As an adult, you can gather corpses for your offspring to use as hosts. Gathering blood can jumpstart the growth of your hatchlings to juveniles, or even send them all the way to adulthood.

antaginfo-blob-unrevealed-title = You haven't revealed your true form yet!

antaginfo-blob-unrevealed-desc = You must succumb to the infection. Find somewhere safe and pop!

antaginfo-blob-title = You are the Blob!

antaginfo-blob-overmind = As the overmind, you can control the blob.

antaginfo-blob-reagent-is = Your blob reagent is:

antaginfo-blob-reagent-pre = The

antaginfo-blob-reagent-post = reagent

antaginfo-blob-basics = The Basics

antaginfo-blob-attacking-name = Attacking

antaginfo-blob-attacking-desc = You can expand, which will attack people, damage objects, or place a Normal Blob if the tile is clear.

antaginfo-blob-placement-name = Placement

antaginfo-blob-placement-core = You will be able to manually place your blob core by pressing the Place Blob Core button in the bottom right corner of the screen.

antaginfo-blob-placement-infection = If you are the blob infection, you can place the core where you are standing by pressing the pop button on the top left corner of the screen.

antaginfo-blob-hud-name = HUD

antaginfo-blob-hud-desc = In addition to the buttons on your HUD, there are a few click shortcuts to speed up expansion and defense.

antaginfo-blob-shortcuts-name = Shortcuts

antaginfo-blob-shortcut-click = Click = Expand Blob

antaginfo-blob-shortcut-middle = Middle Mouse Click = Rally Spores

antaginfo-blob-shortcut-ctrl = Ctrl Click = Create Shield Blob

antaginfo-blob-shortcut-alt = Alt Click = Remove Blob

antaginfo-blob-comms-name = Comms

antaginfo-blob-comms-desc = Attempting to talk will send a message to all other overminds, allowing you to coordinate with them.

antaginfo-blob-minions = Minions

antaginfo-blob-blobbernauts-name = Blobbernauts

antaginfo-blob-blobbernauts-desc = This unit can be produced from factories for a cost. They are hard to kill, powerful, and moderately smart. The factory used to create one will become fragile and briefly unable to produce spores.

antaginfo-blob-spores-name = Spores

antaginfo-blob-spores-desc = Produced automatically from factories, these are weak, but can be rallied to attack enemies. They will also attack enemies near the factory and attempt to zombify corpses.

antaginfo-blob-structures = Structures

antaginfo-blob-structures-intro = Normal Blobs will expand your reach and can be upgraded into special blobs that perform certain functions. Bear in mind that expanding into space has an 80% chance of failing!

antaginfo-blob-structures-upgrade = You can upgrade normal blobs into the following types of blob:

antaginfo-blob-structure-strong-name = Strong Blobs

antaginfo-blob-structure-strong-desc = Strong blobs are expensive but take more damage. In additon, they are fireproof and can block air, use these to protect yourself from station fires.

antaginfo-blob-structure-reflective-name = Reflective Blobs

antaginfo-blob-structure-reflective-desc = Upgrading strong blobs creates reflective blobs, capable of reflecting most projectiles at the cost of reduced resistance to explosions.

antaginfo-blob-structure-resource-name = Resource Blobs

antaginfo-blob-structure-resource-desc = Blobs which produce more resources for you, build as many of these as possible to consume the station. This type of blob must be placed near node blobs or your core to work.

antaginfo-blob-structure-factory-name = Factory Blobs

antaginfo-blob-structure-factory-desc = Blobs that spawn blob spores which will attack nearby enemies. This type of blob must be placed near node blobs or your core to work.

antaginfo-blob-structure-node-name = Node Blobs

antaginfo-blob-structure-node-desc = Blobs which grow, like the core. Like the core it can activate resource and factory blobs.

antaginfo-blob-objectives = Objectives
